AI Self-Healing Framework Overview\par \par # AI Self-Healing Test Framework - Understanding Document\par \par ## Executive Summary\par \par The AI Self-Healing Test Framework is an intelligent test automation solution that automatically adapts when web application elements change. Instead of failing when developers modify button IDs, field names, or page layouts, these tests intelligently find alternative ways to interact with elements, dramatically reducing test maintenance overhead.\par \par ## 🎯 What is AI Self-Healing Testing?\par \par <strong>Traditional Testing Problem:</strong>\par \par - Developer changes: <code><button id="submit-btn"></code> → <code><button id="new-submit-btn"></code>\par \par - Normal test result: <strong>FAILS</strong> <span class="emoji fail">❌</span> "Element not found"\par \par - Maintenance required: Manual test script updates\par \par <strong>AI Self-Healing Solution:</strong>\par \par - Same developer change occurs\par \par - Self-healing test result: <strong>SUCCEEDS</strong> <span class="emoji success">✅</span> "Found button using text 'Submit'"\par \par - Maintenance required: <strong>Zero</strong> - test adapts automatically\par \par ## 🏗️ Framework Architecture\par \par ### **4-Tier Healing Strategy**\par \par ```\par \par Tier 1: Basic Healing\par ├─ Manual fallback strategies\par ├─ Predefined alternative locators\par └─ Simple retry mechanisms\par \par Tier 2: Smart Healing\par ├─ Intelligent strategy generation\par ├─ Element type recognition\par ├─ Pattern-based fallback\par └─ Context-aware locators\par \par Tier 3: AI-Powered Healing\par ├─ GPT-4o integration via Walmart AI Gateway\par ├─ Dynamic locator generation\par ├─ Natural language element description\par └─ Real-time page analysis\par \par Tier 4: Learning & Adaptation\par ├─ Success pattern storage\par ├─ Historical healing data\par ├─ Performance optimization\par └─ Continuous improvement\par \par ```\par \par ## 📚 Framework Components\par \par ### **Core Pyt